A COPYBOOK is a reusable piece of COBOL code that can be included in multiple COBOL programs.

For example, suppose we have a customer record structure.

Copybook: CUSTCOPY
       01 WS-CUSTOMER-RECORD.
          05 WS-CUST-ID   PIC 9(5).
          05 WS-CUST-NAME PIC X(20).
          05 WS-CUST-AGE  PIC 9(3).


Main COBOL program:
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

           COPY CUSTCOPY.

       PROCEDURE DIVISION.

           MOVE 10001 TO WS-CUST-ID.
           MOVE "SAGARA" TO WS-CUST-NAME.
           MOVE 030 TO WS-CUST-AGE.

           DISPLAY WS-CUSTOMER-RECORD.

           STOP RUN.
